The fitness increased from 158 to 188, representing an improvement of approximately 19% over the initial score.

These results demonstrate that local search can improve the arrangement by repeatedly accepting beneficial swaps.

Results may vary when the randomly generated attributes or initial arrangement change.

## Limitations and Possible Improvements

The current implementation has several limitations:

- Local optima:The search may stop improving before reaching the global optimum.
- Single initial solution:The algorithm explores only one search trajectory.
- Greedy acceptance: Candidate arrangements with lower or equal fitness are rejected.
- Random initialization: Different input attributes can produce different outcomes.

Possible improvements include:

- Running hill climbing multiple times with different initial arrangements.
- Implementing simulated annealing to allow occasional acceptance of worse solutions.
- Comparing different mutation operators and iteration counts.
- Comparing hill climbing with evolutionary algorithms using population-based search.

